<title>SPAIN: Spain's labour reform boosts jobs - ministry.</title>
<headline>Spain's labour reform boosts jobs - ministry.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Labour Ministry said on Wednesday that 81,808 job contracts were registered under the regulations of recent labour reforms, effect in May.</p>
<p>Of this figure, 64,981 were permanent contracts, including 49,357 which were conversions from temporary contracts and 15,624 which were first-time permanent contracts.</p>
<p>New training contracts accounted for 16,827 of the total.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
